Hello everyone,

in my current game as a priest, I managed to polymorph my two pet
soldier ants into something useful, at last, after first turning them
into such menacing beasts as a lichen, winter wolf cub, dwarf zombie
and small mimic (and losing my original cat, which turned into a
shocking sphere and exploded in the face of an unlucky kobold, at
least killing him in the process).

They morphed into a silver dragon and a salamander.

Now, with pet management being so annoying (despite the magic whistle,
without which I wouldn't even bother with pets after a certain point
in the game), I will probably only keep one of them, and the question
is which one.

I've had dragons of various colors as pets before, so the silver
dragon would be sort of a standard choice, as he's obviously powerful
overall, will reflect nasty magic stuff and have a boatload of HP once
he's all grown up.

However, the salamander gets an additional attack, is faster than the
dragon, doesn't seem to eat (not sure about that, but I've only seen
the dragon munching on corpses so far) and, most importantly, will use
weapons - probably causing way more damage with them than the dragon
with his bite and claw attacks. Since my priest is neutral, there will
be plenty of artifact weapons available, too.

Which one would you choose, and why? Has anyone here had a pet
salamander before, and if so, how useful did it turn out to be? Which
weapon did you give him?

I've got to take a break from the game for a few days and would be
glad to hear your thoughts and experiences on those pets until I can
continue playing my (rather promising-looking) priest character.

